`FoundationEmbeddingExtractor` loads its model again when a recording comes with another sampling rate, other channels, another channel order or another window length than the one it loaded the model for. It kept the first model, which is built for one montage (channel positions, BIOT's bipolar pairs, BENDR's channel order, LaBraM's channel names) and one window length, so a second recording with the same channels in another order was embedded as if its channels were the first recording's. A model passed to the extractor is used as given.
